1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,150
(Zack:)there's no
one right answer.

2
00:00:06,220 --> 00:00:08,220
(Sheldon:)So...

3
00:00:08,220 --> 00:00:09,820
(Leonard:)you and Zack again, huh?

4
00:00:09,820 --> 00:00:11,760
(Penny:)Yeah, yeah, me
and Zack again.

5
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:13,360
(Zack:)Were we here earlier?

6
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:16,190
(Penny:)Okay, we should,
we should go.

7
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:17,250
(Zack:)Ah, not yet.

8
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:19,610
(Zack:)I want to talk science
with the science dudes.

9
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:23,400
(Howard:)Oh, and the science dudes want
to talk science with you.

10
00:00:24,770 --> 00:00:25,870
(Howard:)What do you want
to talk about--

11
00:00:25,870 --> 00:00:30,010
(Howard:)rocks, dinosaurs, our
friend the beaver?

12
00:00:31,180 --> 00:00:33,510
(Zack:)You know, I saw this great thing
on the Discovery Channel.

13
00:00:33,510 --> 00:00:35,380
(Zack:)Turns out
that if you kill a starfish,

14
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:37,550
(Zack:)it'll just come back to life.

15
00:00:39,350 --> 00:00:41,220
(Sheldon:)Was the starfish
wearing boxer shorts?

16
00:00:41,220 --> 00:00:43,490
(Sheldon:)Because you might have
been watching Nickelodeon.

17
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:49,890
(Zack:)No, I'm almost sure that
it was the Discovery Channel.

18
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:51,160
(Zack:)It was a great show.

19
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:53,330
(Zack:)They also said dolphins
might be smarter than people.

20
00:00:53,330 --> 00:00:56,940
They might be smarter
than some people.

21
00:00:59,070 --> 00:01:01,660
(Zack:)Maybe we can do an
experiment to find out.

22
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:03,110
(Sheldon:)That's easy enough.

23
00:01:03,110 --> 00:01:06,210
(Sheldon:)We'd need a large tank of
water, a hoop to jump through,

24
00:01:06,210 --> 00:01:08,650
(Sheldon:)and a bucket of whatever
bite-sized treats

25
00:01:08,650 --> 00:01:10,780
(Sheldon:)you find tasty.

26
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:19,160
(Zack:)I don't get it.

27
00:01:19,160 --> 00:01:20,590
(Leonard:)A dolphin might.

28
00:01:23,830 --> 00:01:25,200
(Zack:)Oh, I see.

29
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:27,330
(Zack:)You guys are inferring
that I'm stupid.

30
00:01:27,330 --> 00:01:28,600
(Sheldon:)That's not correct.

31
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:31,490
(Sheldon:)We were implying it.

32
00:01:31,490 --> 00:01:33,710
(Sheldon:)You then inferred it.

33
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:39,680
(Zack:)Let's go.

34
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:42,650
(Penny:)You know, for a group of guys

35
00:01:42,650 --> 00:01:45,280
(Penny:)who claim they spent most
of their lives being bullied,

36
00:01:45,280 --> 00:01:46,830
(Penny:)you can be real jerks.

37
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:48,650
(Penny:)Shame on all of you.

38
00:01:50,990 --> 00:01:53,320
(Raj:)What the hell did I do?

39
00:01:54,130 --> 00:01:55,830
(Penny(Opens door again):)You laughed.

40
00:01:57,030 --> 00:02:00,660
♪ Our whole universe
was in a hot, dense state ♪

